  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-bb80fd4f-7fff-e8a9-66f4-849e17a3334f&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed rear roof extensions, by reason of inappropriate scale,detailed design and location, would result in an overbearing, obtrusive and incongruous form of development, to the detriment of the character and appearance of the site(s), the wider terrace and rear street scene of Leadale Road. Therefore, it is considered that the proposed development would be contrary to LP33 policy LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character); policy D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) of The London Plan (adopted 2021), the Council’s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009) and the Stamford Hill Area Action Plan (Publication Version) policy AAP.3 (Residential Extensions and Alterations)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
